.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "void VERUM_ASCON_AEAD128_encrypt (const uint32_t key[4U], const uint32_t nonce[4U], uint8_t * plaintext, uint32_t plaintext_size, const uint8_t * associated_data, uint32_t associated_size, uint32_t authentication_tag[4U])"

.PP
Ascon-AEAD128 authenticated encryption\&. Encrypts \fRplaintext\fP in place and produces a 128-bit authentication tag over the ciphertext and, when \fRVERUM_ASCON_AEAD128_ASSOCIATED_DATA_DEF\fP is defined, over \fRassociated_data\fP as well\&. The operation follows Algorithm 3 of NIST SP 800-232 Section 4\&.1\&.1\&.

.PP
On return, the buffer addressed by \fRplaintext\fP holds the ciphertext of equal length\&. The original plaintext is overwritten and cannot be recovered from \fRplaintext\fP alone\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIkey\fP 128-bit secret key\&. 
.br
\fInonce\fP 128-bit public nonce\&. 
.br
\fIplaintext\fP On entry: plaintext buffer of \fRplaintext_size\fP bytes\&. On return: ciphertext of equal length, written in place\&. 
.br
\fIplaintext_size\fP Length of \fRplaintext\fP in bytes\&. May be zero, in which case no plaintext blocks are processed and the tag covers only associated data\&.
.br
\fIassociated_data\fP Pointer to associated data of \fRassociated_size\fP bytes\&. Authenticated but not encrypted\&. Only present when \fRVERUM_ASCON_AEAD128_ASSOCIATED_DATA_DEF\fP is defined\&. 
.br
\fIassociated_size\fP Length of \fRassociated_data\fP in bytes\&. May be zero\&. Only present when \fRVERUM_ASCON_AEAD128_ASSOCIATED_DATA_DEF\fP is defined\&.
.br
\fIauthentication_tag\fP 128-bit authentication tag produced after finalisation, written as four consecutive 32-bit words\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBPrecondition\fP
.RS 4
\fRkey\fP, \fRnonce\fP, \fRplaintext\fP and \fRauthentication_tag\fP are non-NULL\&. 

.PP
\fRplaintext\fP points to a buffer of at least \fRplaintext_size\fP bytes\&. 

.PP
\fRplaintext\fP and \fRauthentication_tag\fP do not overlap\&. 

.PP
The nonce is used at most once for a given key\&. 
.RE
.PP

