.SS "void VERUM_ASCON_AEAD128_decrypt (const uint32_t key[4U], const uint32_t nonce[4U], uint8_t * ciphertext, uint32_t ciphertext_size, const uint8_t * associated_data, uint32_t associated_size, uint32_t authentication_tag[4U])"

.PP
Ascon-AEAD128 authenticated decryption\&. Decrypts \fRciphertext\fP in place and verifies the 128-bit authentication tag over the plaintext and, when \fRVERUM_ASCON_AEAD128_ASSOCIATED_DATA_DEF\fP is defined, over \fRassociated_data\fP as well\&. The operation follows Algorithm 4 of NIST SP 800-232 Section 4\&.1\&.1\&.

.PP
On return, the buffer addressed by \fRciphertext\fP holds the plaintext of equal length\&. The original ciphertext is overwritten and cannot be recovered from \fRciphertext\fP alone\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIkey\fP 128-bit secret key\&. 
.br
\fInonce\fP 128-bit public nonce\&. 
.br
\fIciphertext\fP On entry: ciphertext buffer of \fRciphertext_size\fP bytes\&. On return: plaintext of equal length, written in place\&. 
.br
\fIciphertext_size\fP Length of \fRciphertext\fP in bytes\&. May be zero, in which case no ciphertext blocks are processed and the tag covers only associated data\&.
.br
\fIassociated_data\fP Pointer to associated data of \fRassociated_size\fP bytes\&. Authenticated but not decrypted\&. Only present when \fRVERUM_ASCON_AEAD128_ASSOCIATED_DATA_DEF\fP is defined\&. 
.br
\fIassociated_size\fP Length of \fRassociated_data\fP in bytes\&. May be zero\&. Only present when \fRVERUM_ASCON_AEAD128_ASSOCIATED_DATA_DEF\fP is defined\&.
.br
\fIauthentication_tag\fP 128-bit authentication tag to verify after finalisation, read as four consecutive 32-bit words\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBPrecondition\fP
.RS 4
\fRkey\fP, \fRnonce\fP, \fRciphertext\fP and \fRauthentication_tag\fP are non-NULL\&. 

.PP
\fRciphertext\fP points to a buffer of at least \fRciphertext_size\fP bytes\&. 

.PP
\fRciphertext\fP and \fRauthentication_tag\fP do not overlap\&. 

.PP
The nonce matches the one used during encryption\&. 
.RE
.PP

